When a step body is inlined, its step-targeted rule comes with it — the step's `## Rules` block
follows the body inside the `## Step:` section, ahead of the step's `## Lessons` block — while the
playbook-targeted rule keeps its own section above the step table.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core: {namespace: fx, path: ~/core-specs}
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/rule/0001-playbook-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Playbook rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-inline]
brief: Playbook brief.
---
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/rule/0002-step-rule.md --
---
type: rule
title: Step rule
status: accepted
targets: [fx-rule-inline/s1]
brief: Step brief.
---
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_lessons/0001_step.md --
---
title: Step lesson
targets: [fx-rule-inline/s1]
---

Step lesson body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-inline/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-rule-inline
title: Rules
summary: Rule injection.
inline_steps: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-inline/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  s1: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-rule-inline/s1/prompt.md --
---
name: s1
summary: Only step.
---

Step body.
